The jog frames on two more machines, beside twp-jog-frame.

trivkins, not homed, with a plane turned 45 degrees about Z: a frame jog
gets the travel a plain jog of an axis not homed gets, one range either
way of where it stands, not the [AXIS_<letter>] limits, so an incremental
jog past them goes and a continuous one runs to one range from its start.

Then a trunnion, xyzac-trt-kins, on the tool centre point type with C at
90 degrees: a machine frame jog moves the slide of its letter alone, X,
Y and Z, and again with A tilted 30 degrees, since the machine does not
turn when the table does; the plane frame with no plane jogs the part's
X, turned with the table onto the Y slide; the tool frame jogs Z on the
Z slide; on the identity type a machine X jog moves X.
